---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="OpenSLM.ai — an initiative for open, accessible, and correctable small language models. Founded by Anivar Aravind."
  ogType="article"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>

  <section class="hero hero--page">
    <div class="container-page hero__inner">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">About this<br />initiative</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">
        OpenSLM.ai is an initiative to make small language models, and the systems
        that run them, open in a way that holds up: inspectable, reproducible, and
        correctable by the people they affect.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-mark" aria-hidden="true">§</div>

  <section class="tail-section">
    <div class="container-page tail-section__inner">
      <p class="tail-paragraph">
        The initiative is founded and initiated by
        <a href="https://anivar.net">Anivar Aravind</a>, a longtime contributor to free
        software, language technology, and digital rights, with a focus on open
        infrastructure for non-English-speaking users.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-grid">
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h4>General inquiries</h4>
          <a href="mailto:hello@openslm.ai">hello@openslm.ai</a>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h4>Endorsement</h4>
          <a href="mailto:endorse@openslm.ai">endorse@openslm.ai</a>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h4>Code and issues</h4>
          <a href="https://github.com/openslm-ai">github.com/openslm-ai</a>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h4>Support the work</h4>
          <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/anivar">github.com/sponsors/anivar</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="tail-paragraph">
        Sponsorship goes to the maintainer rather than to an organisation
        account. OpenSLM is one author and a small number of repositories today,
        and a separate funding entity would add opacity rather than assurance.
        That changes if the work does — a second maintainer, or institutional
        funding, and this becomes an organisation page. Sponsorship buys no
        influence over the accord; it is revised through open process, and
        endorsement is not for sale.
      </p>

      <h3 class="involve-h">Get involved</h3>
      <ul class="involve-list">
        <li>
          Open an issue or pull request on
          <a href="https://github.com/openslm-ai">github.com/openslm-ai</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Send a note to <a href="mailto:hello@openslm.ai">hello@openslm.ai</a> to
          discuss the accord, contribute code, or work on the research.
        </li>
        <li>
          Endorse the accord once endorsement opens after the first wave of
          conversations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/anivar">Sponsor the work</a> to
          keep the specification, tooling, and standards work independent of
          vendor funding.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
